CORE
main.cpp
--cpp20
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ designated base element: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ two designators: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
N5008 [dcl.init.aggr]/3.1, /5: in `D d{{.a = 2}, 4}' the base element A
is initialized from a designated-initializer-list: a from 2, b from its
default member initializer, c value-initialized.  The aggregate-with-base
path assigned the designated initializers positionally (bin53: an
invariant violation in symex).  They are now matched to the members by
name.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept this program, and it fails only its
WRONG assertion.
